# Test case inspired by Figure 14 of the TUSQH paper (Shawcroft et al. IMR 2025).
#
# Geometry: outer rectangle with TWO interior islands arranged horizontally
# so they form an archipelago near the bottom. The sub-cell VFs of the
# boundary edges between each island and the outer rectangle should be
# interior (above threshold), making them bridge candidates.
#
# Expected behavior with -J:
#   - bridge-joining connects the components into one mesh
#   - small components (with < -L cells) are dropped
#
# Expected behavior WITHOUT -J:
#   - multiple disconnected components remain
#
# Vertices: 12 (4 outer + 4 + 4 for each of two islands)
# All polygons are CCW (winding number convention).
# Outer: (0,0)-(3,0)-(3,1)-(0,1) - large domain
# Island A: (0.4,0.4)-(0.8,0.4)-(0.8,0.7)-(0.4,0.7)
# Island B: (1.6,0.4)-(2.0,0.4)-(2.0,0.7)-(1.6,0.7)

12 2 0 0
 1   0.0   0.0
 2   3.0   0.0
 3   3.0   1.0
 4   0.0   1.0
 5   0.4   0.4
 6   0.8   0.4
 7   0.8   0.7
 8   0.4   0.7
 9   1.6   0.4
10   2.0   0.4
11   2.0   0.7
12   1.6   0.7
